    "Scouting Notes": "As an amateur was seen as a high on base threat who makes a lot of contact and has sharp strike zone discipline.\n Mostly a line drive hitter with gap power. \n Struggled a decent amount with a pretty aggressive assignment to Low A (which shows how the Brewers view him), but had a solid finish to his season in the ACL.\n Pro ball has shown more of an affinity for strikeouts than expected and not showing a ton of XBH pop at full season ball.\n Better than average runner\n Likely a third baseman defensively, where he has good hands and footwork\n Still definitely something there, but not unfair to worry about the performance in full season, and higher K numbers than expected.",
